france was the fourth nation to acquire  nuclear weapons  the first three had built theirs off of  the work done during the manhattan  project with the usa doing the leg work  the uss are stealing secrets from the  u.s fire espionage and the uk via  essentially copying america's homework  but france's route becoming a nuclear  power was different and fraught with its  own problems  so how did france do it how did france  acquire nuclear weapons  so as of the end of world war ii france  wasn't completely new to nuclear  technology and some of its own  scientists had worked on the manhattan  project under the british umbrella  so at the end of the 1940s the french  government started a nuclear program  with the help of israeli scientists  whose aid was fundamentally moving the  project along  at first the nuclear program was  civilian in nature and france very  quickly became a world leader in the  building of nuclear reactors  naturally having civilian nuclear power  meant that nuclear armament was much  easier because of all of that spare  refined nuclear material just lying  around  in 1956 after the suez crisis france was  left internationally humiliated and felt  that neither the usa nor the uk could be  relied upon to use their nuclear weapons  in the defense of france  as such the french sought to build their  own and briefly actively worked with  west germany and italy to build nuclear  arsenals for all three  this was scrapped when charles de gaulle  became president in late 1958 since he  wanted france's nuclear program to be as  self-sufficient as possible  a side effect of this decision was that  unlike the british program the french  one was incredibly expensive and was a  major drain on other parts of the french  military  and the reason for this was that unlike  when britain began building nuclear  weapons the us was hostile to the idea  not hostile enough to do anything about  it but american leadership made it clear  that it felt that france did not need  its own nuclear weapons  and as such they got zero help from the  us which increased the cost of the  program  so why allow britain but not france well  it was because france's nuclear strategy  was going to be fundamentally different  from britain's  you see britain had largely agreed to  maintain the same deterrent policy as  the united states  one which called for response in kind no  escalation and no first strike  whereas france had different plans  french leadership believed that an  invasion by the ussr could only be  stopped with a nuclear retaliation  meaning the soviets would have a choice  invade and lose half of ukraine and  belarus or retaliate with their own  nukes  and a soviet nuclear attack would then  force a response from the uk and the usa  since radiation doesn't care for borders  which for the french meant that they  could effectively force the use of  british and american arsenals if they  wanted to  you can see why the two weren't so keen  french and israeli scientists continued  in collaboration until france had  constructed and tested its first bomb in  1960.  the test was carried out in algeria and  was probably followed by israeli  scientists being dismissed from the  programme and also a lot of grumbling  from the ussr and mild annoyance from  the usa  algeria gained its independence in 1962  but the french continued to test there  until the mid-1960s where they changed  their primary testing site to french  polynesia  by 1964 france had its first operational  nuclear weapons and would go on to  expand its arsenal throughout the cold  war  and thus the french had despite varying  levels of opposition from the other  nuclear powers joined the club as its  fourth member  i hope you enjoyed this episode and  thank you for watching with a special  thanks to my patrons  james bissonette kelly moneymaker danny  maloney marvin cassell the pastry  section rob waterhouse  moe aaron the white james castaneda  jordan longley gustav swann marcus asner  jerry lamdin  rasheed ali cooling castleman spinning  three plates david silverman maggie  paxkowski  coppertone izzy spencer lightfoot fobo  joe matthew shipley  robert wetzel lexi schwinn and winston k  wood
 

